  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Rights-Based Solutions and Consular Assistance for Vulnerable Migrants in Libya through the Migrant Resource and Response Mechanism (MRRM) and Delivery of Public Services (Embassy and Passport Authority Support)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to contribute to advancing rights-based solutions to address the needs of vulnerable migrants in Libya, consistent with the United Nations Sustainable Development and Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF &#x2013; outcome 2 on migration  management, for which IOM is co-lead) adopted jointly by the Government of Libya and the United Nations agencies and entered into force in 2023. In addition, this initiative is in line with the IOM Response Plan for the Mediterranean and Beyond. and also in line with IOM Libya country strategy 2021-2024.Through the first outcome of this project, IOM will continue its critical interventions to directly support migrants, including persons who have experienced distress, multiple displacement or challenges in accessing essential services. Approximately 9,000 migrants living in urban areas as well as vulnerable cases from host communities will benefit from a comprehensive approach that bring together a wide range of services and needs based assistance in one mechanism. Through the second outcome of this project, complementary to the first one in relation to promoting consular capacity for assistance to their nationals, as well as facilizing issuance of travel documents for assistance via VHR, IOM will continue addressing a recognised capacity gap in the provision of robust consular support services for stranded migrants in Libya as well as for the Libyan Passport Authority (PA).</narrative>
  </description>
